[BorrowScript](https://github.com/alshdavid/BorrowScript) is a Rust inspired Borrow Checker with TypeScript inspired Syntax. It adds [ownership operators](https://github.com/alshdavid/BorrowScript#ownership-operators) that looks like a related approach to the suggested `out` operator (see `write` operator and [this](https://github.com/alshdavid/BorrowScript/issues/23) issue regarding a current typo in the readme in the `write` example). Keep in mind that BorrowScript is overall a different language that compiles to static binaries. For example, `string` is mutable. Hence, the example of the `write` operator looks like this

```typescript
function writeFoo(write foo: string) {
  foo.push('bar')
  console.log(foo) // "foobar"
}
```

